# LMD-GHOST Fork-Choice Estimator — Formal Verification
#
# Mechanizes the GHOST-style heaviest-subtree fork-choice estimator and the
# properties on which its consensus-critical correctness rests: score
# order-independence (no fork from validator-iteration order), the (score DESC,
# hash ASC) tie-break TOTAL order that makes the ranked output node-identical
# (S1 fork-prevention), the LMD upward argmax descent's termination and
# heaviest-child selection, the parent-count / parent-depth truncation that
# preserves the ghost main parent, the slashing invalid-message filter (T-10),
# and the "Rocq assumes what Rust enforces" seams (validation ⇒ wf DAG; honest
# fork-choice parents pass the validator's bound-check — validators do NOT
# recompute fork choice, they range-check declared parents).
#
# Source: f1r3node-rust/casper/src/rust/{estimator,validate}.rs,
#         casper/src/rust/engine/multi_parent_casper/snapshot.rs,
#         casper/src/rust/util/{proto_util,dag_operations}.rs,
#         shared/src/rust/shared/list_ops.rs (sort_by_with_decreasing_order).
#
# Zero `Admitted`. No custom `Axiom` or `Parameter`. Section `Variable`/
# `Hypothesis` (GuardBridge, as in finalized_floor) become premises of the
# closed term, NOT axioms.
#
# NOTE — a `Recovery`-analog (finalized_floor/theories/Recovery.v) is
# DELIBERATELY OMITTED here: fork choice is a STATELESS re-derivation each round
# (estimator.rs::tips recomputes from the DAG + latest messages every call),
# so there is no effect-application / idempotence obligation to discharge.
#
# Module dependency graph (-> = "depends on"):
#
#   Foundation            (standalone: DAG, block numbers, parents, ancestry, height bound)
#   Score      -> Foundation                 (per-validator weight, supporting-chain scores)
#   Filter     -> Foundation                 (T-10 slashed/invalid latest-message filter)
#   TieBreak   -> Foundation                 (the (score DESC, hash ASC) TOTAL order + unique sort — S1)
#   Lca        -> Foundation                 (LCUA common-ancestor + depth cutoff filter)
#   Rank       -> Foundation Score TieBreak   (LMD upward argmax descent: terminates, picks heaviest)
#   Bound      -> Foundation Rank            (parent-count cap: keeps the ghost main parent; typed empty err)
#   GuardBridge-> Foundation Rank Bound Filter Score TieBreak  (validation⇒wf; honest parents validate)
#   MainTheorem-> all                        (four end-to-end capstones, axiom-free)

